{
  "label": "prop:milne-finite-quotient",
  "lean_status": "empty",
  "last_comment": "Commits 81a9fc6f53, b599860a21, and b897c8243a prove characteristic-free denominator clearing for finite-group invariants, the canonical ring equivalence (A^G)[1/b] = (A[1/b])^G, the corresponding quotient basic-open isomorphism, and an Arrow isomorphism comparing the restricted affine quotient map with the fixed-subring inclusion on that localization. This advances the first unmet producer to quotient-side opens for pairwise stable-chart intersections, canonical overlap/triple transitions, and their cocycle. The source proposition remains EMPTY: no Scheme.GlueData, global sheaf quotient, arbitrary-target universal property, or free-action etaleness is claimed."
}

